## VERDICT RATIONALE
Two of three families the ruling required — sortable headers, nav
rows/tiles' modal-open behavior — are fixed correctly and independently
verified live. The third (KPI tiles) fixes keyboard reachability
correctly but its chosen pattern (`role="button"` wrapping a div that,
on one data-dependent branch, contains a real focusable `<a>`) introduces
a NEW, axe-detectable WCAG 4.1.2 (`nested-interactive`, serious impact)
violation on the Budget tile's "no target set" state — proven against the
actual attempt-2 markup and the actual `dashboard.js`, and proven absent
on master's equivalent (pre-`role`) markup, so this is content this
attempt's own fix newly broke, not a carried-over defect. This state is
common (any household without a What-If budget target) and is the exact
branch the worker's own manifest names as the reason a native `<button>`
was not used — the worker reasoned about this branch and still landed
on a structurally invalid nesting. FAIL.

Scope for attempt 3 (do not re-open the other two families, which pass):
fix the Budget tile only — e.g. don't put `role="button"`/`tabindex="0"`
on the outer div when it can contain the `<a href="/whatif">` (make the
"Set a budget" link the tile's sole interactive affordance for that
branch and drop the click-to-open-modal behavior there), or restructure
so the link sits outside the `role="button"` region, or another pattern
that does not nest a second interactive control inside the `role="button"`
element. Re-verify keyboard activation of both the tile and the link
after the fix, and re-run axe against the "no target set" branch
specifically (the fixture gap that hid this — force the state via a
throwaway data copy with no budget target configured, not the default
verify-server data).

## OBSERVATIONS (not blocking, for the ledger/backlog)
- The verify-server's default fixture data (and, apparently, every prior
  U6/U7 axe oracle's fixture data) never exercises the dashboard's
  "no budget target configured" state. Worth a follow-up: extend the U6/
  U7 oracle's data setup (or add a second fixture) so this state is
  scanned by the standing sitewide sweep rather than requiring a manual
  isolated probe, the same lesson as rulings U-2026-09-03h and
  U-2026-09-04j/k (hidden state ⇒ hidden defects).
- Modal `role="dialog"`/`aria-modal`/focus-trap gap on kpi-detail,
  kpi-month-detail, major-expense-drilldown stays U15 scope per the
  ruling; not re-litigated here, no regression found.
- `major-expenses.html`'s bare `<th data-sort-key>` headers remain
  unchanged by this attempt (pre-existing, U15 scope per attempt-1's
  verdict).

